---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="Privacy Policy - Wi-Fi Camera for PC - Logicpath Systems"
    description="Privacy Policy for Wi-Fi Camera for PC (com.logicpathsystems.wificamerapc) by Logicpath Systems. Effective 13 October 2026."
>
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                        <strong>Wi-Fi Camera for PC</strong> (<code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06); padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.95em;">com.logicpathsystems.wificamerapc</code>)
                    </p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
                        <strong>Developer:</strong> Logicpath Systems · <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a>
                    </p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
                        <strong>Effective Date:</strong> 13 October 2026
                    </p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <div class="summary-box" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary); background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                        <h2 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Summary</h2>
                        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                            Wi-Fi Camera for PC sends your phone's camera and microphone directly to a browser on your own local network. Your video and audio never go to the developer or to the internet. The app has no account. It shows ads through Google AdMob and measures app usage with Google Firebase Analytics, which collect some device and usage data as described below.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <h2>1. Camera and Microphone</h2>
                    <p>
                        Camera and microphone access is used only while you have started streaming, to show the preview on the phone and to send live video and audio to the PC browser you connect. Nothing is recorded or saved on the phone, and the video and audio are not shared with Google or anyone else.
                    </p>

                    <h2>2. Local Network</h2>
                    <p>
                        The app runs a small web server on your Wi-Fi address while streaming is on. A browser can watch only after entering the 6-digit PIN shown on the phone. Video and audio travel directly between the phone and that browser over your network.
                    </p>

                    <h2>3. Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
                    <p>
                        The app shows ads from Google AdMob: a banner at the bottom of some screens, an app open ad when you return to the app, and occasionally a full-screen ad right after you stop streaming. Full-screen ads never appear while you are streaming. To show and measure ads and to prevent fraud, Google may collect your device's advertising ID, IP address, approximate location derived from it, device and app information, and how you interact with ads. Where the law requires it, ads are personalised only with your consent; otherwise non-personalised ads are shown. See how Google uses data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>
                    </p>

                    <h2>4. Analytics (Google Firebase Analytics)</h2>
                    <p>
                        Firebase Analytics records how the app is used, such as app opens, starting and stopping streaming, the chosen video orientation, and screens viewed, together with an app instance ID, device model, operating system, app version, language and approximate location (country or region). It does not record the PIN, IP addresses of your devices, the address you open on your PC, or any video or audio. Firebase privacy information: <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a>
                    </p>

                    <h2>5. Consent and Your Choices</h2>
                    <p>
                        If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, the app asks for your consent through Google's consent message before ads or analytics storage are used, and you can change your choice at any time under <strong>More &rarr; Privacy choices</strong>. On any Android phone you can reset or delete your advertising ID, or opt out of personalised ads, in <strong>Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads</strong> (or <strong>Settings &rarr; Privacy &rarr; Ads</strong>).
                    </p>

                    <h2>6. Sharing and Transfers</h2>
                    <p>
                        The developer does not sell your data. Data collected by AdMob and Firebase Analytics is processed by Google as described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Google Privacy Policy (https://policies.google.com/privacy)</a> and may be processed on servers outside your country.
                    </p>

                    <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
                    <p>
                        Analytics data is kept only for the retention period set in Google Analytics and is then deleted. Advertising data is retained by Google under its own policies. The app itself keeps no history of your streams.
                    </p>

                    <h2>8. Snapshots and Recordings</h2>
                    <p>
                        Snapshots and recordings are created by the PC browser and saved on that PC. The app does not keep copies.
                    </p>

                    <h2>9. Notifications and Background Use</h2>
                    <p>
                        While streaming, the app shows a notification and keeps the camera, microphone and Wi-Fi active so streaming continues with the screen off. Tap <strong>Stop</strong> in the notification to end it.
                    </p>

                    <h2>10. Data Stored on the Phone</h2>
                    <p>
                        The app stores simple settings on the phone, such as whether you accepted the responsible-use notice, how many times the app has been opened and when an ad was last shown (to limit how often ads appear). Google's SDKs store their own identifiers and your consent choice on the phone.
                    </p>

                    <h2>11. Security</h2>
                    <p>
                        Video and audio are encrypted in transit by WebRTC, but the web page, PIN and control messages are sent over plain HTTP on your network. Use the app only on a Wi-Fi network you trust, and do not share the PIN.
                    </p>

                    <h2>12. Responsible Use</h2>
                    <p>
                        Only stream or record people with their consent. Recording or monitoring others without permission may be illegal where you live. You are responsible for how you use this app.
                    </p>

                    <h2>13. Children and Age Requirement</h2>
                    <p>
                        The app is intended for adults aged 18 and over. It is not directed at anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from people under 18. If you believe someone under 18 has used the app, contact us and we will help remove any related data.
                    </p>

                    <h2>14. Changes</h2>
                    <p>
                        If this policy changes, the updated version will be shown in the app and on the policy web page with a new effective date.
                    </p>

                    <h2>15. Contact</h2>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Logicpath Systems</strong><br />
                        Email: <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a>
                    </p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2, .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .legal-content h2 {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content h3 {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }
    
    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul, .legal-content table {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content table td, .legal-content table th {
        border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    }
</style>
